       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you meant.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose**, if you meant a different dose.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that explicitly and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it as written with that note."
